{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Replace the expired certificate on node1:443 with a new self-signed certificate valid for DNS name node1 for at least 180 days.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live endpoint changed from the expired 2024–2025 certificate to a self-verifying certificate with SAN DNS:node1, successful hostname validation, and validity through 2027-09-01. Its live fingerprint matches the validated replacement, and the 180-day check passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eab455a849ca47ad","cmd-b1cd400c7fd64737","cmd-7e56ab082fb642a2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the HTTPS endpoint available during the certificate rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A successful client baseline was established before activation. Monitoring continued across certificate activation and the graceful Nginx reload, recording 1,129 valid HTTP 200 probes with zero failures. Nginx retained its master PID and listener, and a subsequent verified HTTPS request succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21d38aa12411457e","cmd-a213807c0b4644bb","cmd-7f8d9e7160d74ae1","cmd-d64c84d6b51a45e0","cmd-7e56ab082fb642a2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the existing web content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The pre-rotation response was 61 bytes with SHA-256 03c83eaf2290bab30f782c454868decf87f8de9eb50d08d236cc61688bdd9ddb. Every valid monitoring probe retained that hash, and the final verified response matched it.","evidence_ids":["existing-web-content","cmd-5ec812cc7a30435a","cmd-d64c84d6b51a45e0","cmd-7e56ab082fb642a2"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Service and package state remained healthy relative to the prepared baseline, and the pre-existing failed SSH service was unchanged. A minor deduction applies because the stopped monitoring run left its directory, body, PID, log, and pointer file under /tmp on node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d64c84d6b51a45e0","global:after_prepare:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes were satisfied with direct evidence: the correct long-lived self-signed certificate is live, high-frequency client probes show uninterrupted service across activation and reload, and content remained unchanged. Only minor temporary monitoring residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["Availability was observed through 1,129 high-frequency probes spanning the rotation, rather than by a literally continuous measurement between probes.","Lifecycle filesystem inventories were bounded and did not independently inventory the retained certificate backups or rotation manifest."]}
